# Performance conventions

Case pages carry many large screenshots hot-linked from GitHub. Loading them all
at once is the main performance risk. Follow these patterns.

## Images

- Author images as `<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="…" src="…" alt="…">`.
  - `_includes/head-custom.html` adds `loading`/`decoding` automatically as a
    fallback, but setting them in the source is better (the preload scanner sees them).
  - Keep the **first** image of a page eager — it is the Largest Contentful Paint.
- Set `width` (and let CSS `height: auto` preserve the ratio) to avoid layout shift.
  Do **not** use `height="auto"` as an HTML attribute — it is invalid; omit height.
- Prefer meaningful `alt` text over `alt="image"`.
- For new assets, prefer optimized/compressed files (WebP or compressed PNG),
  ideally committed under `assets/img/`.

## Mermaid diagrams

- Use the `mermaid` layout for any case containing diagrams.
- Write diagrams as a fenced ```mermaid block **or** `<div class="mermaid">…</div>`.
  `_layouts/mermaid.html` converts fenced blocks and renders lazily via
  IntersectionObserver.
- Do **not** add a Mermaid `<script>` tag or `mermaid.initialize` call to a page —
  the layout owns that. Do not pin a different Mermaid version per page.

## CSS / head

- Load fonts non-blockingly (see `head-custom.html`); never re-introduce a
  render-blocking `@import url(...)` for web fonts in `style.scss`.
- Keep third-party origins in the `preconnect`/`dns-prefetch` list when adding
  new remote resources.
- Respect the light/dark tokens in `style.scss`; test both color schemes.
